I just want to pre-empt the reply that I am expecting now.  'Geodesic dome'
is not a concept of English which is ambigous and requires many different
words in Lojban.

This is so because: "A geodesic dome is an almost spherical structure based
on a network of struts arranged on great circles (geodesics) lying
approximately on the surface of a sphere. The geodesics intersect to form
triangular elements that have local triangular rigidity and yet also
distribute the stress across the entire structure.   The edges of the
triangles create "geodesics," great circles of a sphere, to distribute
stress across the sphere. (The use of patterns of triangles to approximate
either a rougher or smoother shape is also fundamental to computer
graphics.)" http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geodesic_dome

A geodesic dome thus means: a dome composed of geodesics.

Why can't their be a compound word in Lojban that means geodesic
(triangle-circles?) and a root word that means dome???  I'd even settle for
a compound word for dome too if it were only composed of two other words.
(half-circle-dwelling?)

Otherwise Lojban is making a fairly simple concept overly complex I feel.

